sequenceDiagram
  participant G as Grove / caller
  participant R as Rust front process
  participant W as Policy worker
  participant D as Record store
  participant H as Harness
  G->>R: Kind, prompt, parameters + terminal, cwd, environment
  R->>R: Read owner settings: bounds, grants, record directory
  R->>W: Fresh env, private start directory, bounded request with the prompt, null stdin
  opt Dynamic dispatch, the owner's own code
    W->>W: Start a deciding agent in the caller's cwd, wait, reap
  end
  W-->>R: select's result: command + labels + reason, or a refusal
  R->>R: Reap worker, validate the result's shape, resolve the program
  alt Inspect
    R-->>G: Proposal + bounds + command, no harness or run receipt
  else Run
    R->>D: Durable handoff-attempt record
    alt Write fails or cancellation observed
      R-->>G: Nonzero refusal, no harness
    else Admission succeeds
      R->>H: Spawn as its own job: entry signal state, terminal, exit channel, run ID
      Note over R,H: The front stays the parent, its handlers still installed
      H->>R: Exit signal: harness-dispatch exit creates the channel
      R->>H: Grace, then TERM, kill-grace, KILL on the harness's group
      H-->>R: Reaped: exit code or signal
      R->>R: Take the terminal back, restore its modes
      R->>D: End observation: execution confirmed, ending, exit, duration
      R-->>G: Ending file, end notice, exit per the ending
    end
  end
  Note over D: A dispatch killed mid-run leaves its attempt as it stood
